WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:12.340
It's very rarely used but the word “nibble”
means half of a computer byte.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.020
In Bolivia, llama droppings are used to purify
water.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:23.300
To kit yourself out as a real-life Batman
would cost about $300 million.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:29.270
18% of the average American's income is spent
on transportation.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:35.130
Chemicals caused female munitions workers
in the First World War to give birth to yellow

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.989
babies.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:42.600
There are more stars in the universe than
words have been spoken by all of the humans

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.550
who have ever lived.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:50.379
A day on the International Space Station is
one and a half hours long.

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:56.929
Only six out of 22 crocodile species present
any danger to humans.

00:00:56.929 --> 00:01:04.199
Until 1900, visitors to Stonehenge were given
chisels so they could chip off a souvenir.

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:11.270
There are more species of plant on Cape Town's
Table Mountain than in the whole of the UK.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:16.979
The Queen's staff get to choose their own
Christmas presents, which must be worth between

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.320
£20 and £25.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.759
Picasso painted using ordinary house paint.

00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:29.590
The United States has never lost a war in
which donkeys were used.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:36.789
It is cheaper to send Scottish cod to China
to be filleted and sent back again than to

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:39.630
fillet the fish in Scotland.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.229
Heineken beer is designed to foam for precisely
five minutes.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:51.409
In 19th century Britain, attempting to commit
suicide was against the law and was punishable

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:55.749
by death.

